course: dictionary
lesson: 321
title: Feelings in words: anger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anger is a strong feeling. You feel it when something seems unfair, wrong or hurtful, and it can make you want to shout or hit. Read the words around it to be sure: «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the body ready to fight: the heart beats fast, the face goes hot and the fists clench.»
explain: Those clues show the body getting ready for a fight: a fast heart, a hot face, clenched fists. So anger is a strong, physical feeling. The thinking part of the brain takes a few seconds to catch up, which is why you can act before you have thought.
explain: Feeling anger is not bad in itself. What matters is what you do with it. «People can be angry at a little sister, but hurting people is not okay, so the anger needs a safe way out: running, drawing, punching a pillow, talking.»
fact: Anger is the strong feeling you have when you think something is unfair, wrong or hurtful.
fact: To anger someone means to make them angry.
fact: Anger is a normal feeling; what matters is what you do with it.
fact: Safe ways to handle anger include stopping to breathe slowly, counting to ten, walking away, talking about it, or drawing or moving your body.
fact: Hitting, breaking things or hurting people with words is not okay, even when you are angry.
exercise: «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the body ready to fight.» What is anger? | Very happy because of a present | *The strong feeling you have when something seems unfair or hurtful | Sleepy after a long day
exercise: What does «to anger someone» mean? | *To make someone angry | To give someone a present | To make someone laugh | To make someone sleepy
exercise: Which is a safe way to handle anger? | Breaking a toy | Shouting at a friend | Hitting a wall | *Walking away and taking a slow breath
test: «People can be angry at a little sister, but hurting people is not okay.» What is a safe way out for anger? | *Drawing or talking about it | Hurting someone with words | Breaking things | Slamming every door in the house
test: Priya says anger is bad and must never be felt. Is she right? | Yes, so hide it always | Yes, only grown-ups may feel anger | *No, anger is a normal feeling; what matters is what you do with it
exam: Which of these is a good way to calm down when you feel anger? | Hitting your brother | *Stop, breathe slowly and count to ten | Shouting until you cannot stop | Breaking something you own
